<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haifa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haifa is a port city in northern Israel on the Bay of Haifa, at the foot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-carmel">Mount Carmel</a>. A small town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, it was captured by the crusaders in 1100 and became a minor lordship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>. It grew rapidly from the late 19th century with the railway and harbour, and is now one of Israel's largest cities and its main seaport.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haifa.jpg" alt="Haifa" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: . Ray in Manila · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Hanging_Gardens_of_Haifa,_Israel_(50099173503)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
